Patch 16 -- native ARM replacement for the game's x87 dither converter.

SCOPE WARNING: this is a working-tree diff of four files that patches 04-15 also
touch, so it carries their hunks too. The part that is patch 16 is everything
naming mgs2_native_dither / mgs2_dither_* / mgs2_indirect_alternate.

WHAT IT REPLACES

mgs2_sse_rg353vs_port.exe+0x50dae1: float RGBA -> packed RGBA8 with a 4x4
ordered dither, one pixel at a time in scalar x87. Four unattended captures put
44.7% of the main thread's CPU during the 4-7 s post-load freeze in this one
function, ~4.2 s of the 14.2 s of long stalls in a 200 s capture.

Measured: two ABBA cycles, eight autoload runs, one environment variable apart.
Off 18539/18035/21871/19083, on 16427/15839/11461/16143 -- every on-run faster
than every off-run, exact p ~= 0.03, -4.4 s per load (23%).

TWO THINGS THAT ARE NOT OBVIOUS

1. getAlternate() is consulted only for DIRECT rel32 branches. This function is
   a C++ virtual method -- its constructor writes vtable 0x98fc28 -- so it is
   reached through LinkNext(), which looks only in the alternates hash. The
   first build armed the bridge and intercepted nothing for an entire run.
   Hence mgs2_indirect_alternate(), called from LinkNext and deliberately
   narrower than the whole matcher chain, which has no business in that path.

2. The guest sets x87 RC=11 before the loop. That is not "FISTP truncates": RC
   is in the control word and governs every x87 rounding, including the FADDS
   and the FSTPS that narrows to single precision. Rounding those to nearest
   puts 127.99999991 exactly on 128.0f and returns one more than the guest.
   harness/dither/x87_oracle.c runs the real instruction sequence on the build
   host's real x87 and found 24 such cases in 8 million inputs; zero after
   fesetround(FE_TOWARDZERO) around the loop, at both PC=53 and PC=64.

   On-device differential testing does not work here and the reason is
   structural: calling the original from inside the bridge makes the dynarec own
   a block for that address, after which indirect calls stop consulting the hook
   and the run compares one call instead of 16384. Verify mode is retained
   (MGS2_BOX86_NATIVE_DITHER=2) but it is not the oracle.

The self-test carries one probe -- 254.5/255 with dither 0.5 -- that gives 254
under truncation and 255 under round-to-nearest, so it fails loudly if the
rounding mode stops being applied on ARM.

Gated by MGS2_BOX86_NATIVE_DITHER, self-tested before the bridge is published,
matched on an exact 48-byte prologue that is unique in the image's .text.

SHIPPED in FINALPLAY10 as box86-island63-fp10.

